WEBVTT

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:01.901
Modifiers.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:05.350
An intro phrase describes the first noun after the comma.

00:00:06.877 --> 00:00:08.602
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:12.277
The sentence starts with a describing phrase, then a comma.

00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:14.551
And the choices start with different nouns.

00:00:15.593 --> 00:00:19.627
It's testing whether the description sits right next to what it describes.

00:00:20.677 --> 00:00:21.927
Here's the method.

00:00:21.927 --> 00:00:23.702
Read the intro phrase.

00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:25.902
Who or what is it describing?

00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:28.202
Put that noun right after the comma.

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:30.302
And watch out for possessives.

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:34.121
Morrison's novels makes novels the subject, not Morrison.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:40.085
Rule one: an intro phrase describes the very first noun after the comma.

00:00:40.085 --> 00:00:42.160
The rain wasn't walking to school.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.100
I was.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.432
So I comes first.

00:00:45.506 --> 00:00:48.546
Rule two: whoever did the action comes first.

00:00:48.546 --> 00:00:50.896
A conclusion didn't test the samples.

00:00:50.896 --> 00:00:52.253
The researchers did.

00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:56.539
Rule three: a possessive shifts the subject.

00:00:56.539 --> 00:01:01.814
Morrison's novels makes novels the subject, and novels weren't raised in Ohio.

00:01:01.814 --> 00:01:03.023
Morrison was.

00:01:04.081 --> 00:01:05.431
Let's try one.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.331
Born in Guatemala in nineteen thirty-nine.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:10.031
That describes a person.

00:01:10.031 --> 00:01:11.491
The work wasn't born.

00:01:11.491 --> 00:01:13.106
Her novels weren't born.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.656
And it wasn't born.

00:01:14.656 --> 00:01:18.711
Margarita Carrera was born, so she goes right after the comma.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.102
The answer is C.

00:01:21.169 --> 00:01:23.094
Watch out for the possessive.

00:01:23.094 --> 00:01:28.867
The person's name is right there in the answer, but with an apostrophe s, it isn't the subject.

00:01:29.911 --> 00:01:31.791
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.856
How to spot it.

00:01:32.856 --> 00:01:34.181
The three steps.

00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:35.286
The rules.

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:36.336
And the trap.

00:01:36.336 --> 00:01:39.101
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
